  "summary": "Malicious code in bnpl-blocks-atom-bnpl-loader (npm)",
  "details": "On require, the package executes setup.js, a remote binary download-and-execute dropper. It fetches a platform-specific binary over HTTPS from Cloudflare Workers hosts oob-worker[.]cf101-adf[.]workers[.]dev, oob-worker[.]cf102-baf[.]workers[.]dev, oob-worker[.]cf99-9b3[.]workers[.]dev, and oob-worker[.]cf100-416[.]workers[.]dev (paths /pkg/package, /pkg/package-arm64, /pkg/loader_mac, /pkg/package.exe), with a DNS TXT chunked-transfer fallback from the domains c[.]sdk[.]dl[.]wel1[.]ru, ext[.]dl[.]wel1[.]ru, pkg[.]dl[.]wel1[.]ru, and net[.]dl[.]wel1[.]ru. The downloaded binary is written to /tmp or the Windows temp directory under a random name (.cache_\u003chex\u003e or dotnet_diag_\u003chex\u003e.exe) and launched detached (cmd.exe /c start /b on Windows, /bin/sh -c on Unix), so it runs in the background and outlives the parent process.",
